From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 23:59:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd-mbhc-v2: fix double release of the
 MICB_ENABLE vote in wcd_correct_swch_plug()

wcd_mbhc_adc_detect_plug_type() takes exactly one MICB_ENABLE vote
before scheduling correct_plug_swch. wcd_correct_swch_plug() is
supposed to release exactly that one vote with a matching
MICB_DISABLE, but it currently releases it twice on two of its exit
paths:

 - the hs_detect_work_stop early exit calls wcd_micbias_disable()
   (which itself issues MICB_DISABLE) and then falls through to the
   "exit:" label, which unconditionally issues another MICB_DISABLE;

 - a plug_type of MBHC_PLUG_TYPE_HEADPHONE hits the same unconditional
   MICB_DISABLE at "exit:" and then, a few lines later, calls
   wcd_micbias_disable() again for the same reason.

(A headphone plug that also stops mid-detection takes both paths and
releases the single vote three times.)

mbhc_micbias_control() is a manual counter, not an atomic refcount
with a floor: mbhc_cb->mbhc_micbias_control's backing store
(wcd->sysclk_users in wcd934x) has no protection against being driven
negative. Once one of these double-releases has happened, the counter
never returns to zero on disable (it print/decrements from 0 to -1 and
stops there, so the disable branch never runs and the codec bias/MCLK
never powers down) and never reaches 1 on enable either (it goes from
-1 to 0, so the enable branch that reprograms the clock never runs).

Fix it by tracking whether this call has already released the vote
and skipping the redundant release(s), instead of removing
MICB_DISABLE from wcd_micbias_disable() -- that helper has other,
unrelated callers (e.g. wcd_mbhc_report_plug_removal()) that rely on
it being the sole release for their own, separately-taken vote.

No behaviour other than the vote count changes: enable_irq() and the
rest of the HEADPHONE-branch cleanup still run unconditionally.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.c
index 26ebcdadeb7d..b4d5b1ffdc7f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd-mbhc-v2.c
@@ -1154,6 +1154,7 @@ static void wcd_correct_swch_plug(struct work_struct *work)
 	int output_mv, cross_conn, hs_threshold, try = 0, micbias_mv;
 	bool is_spl_hs = false;
 	bool is_pa_on;
+	bool micbias_disabled = false;
 	int ret;
 
 	mbhc = container_of(work, struct wcd_mbhc, correct_plug_swch);
@@ -1218,6 +1219,7 @@ static void wcd_correct_swch_plug(struct work_struct *work)
 	while (!time_after(jiffies, timeout)) {
 		if (mbhc->hs_detect_work_stop) {
 			wcd_micbias_disable(mbhc);
+			micbias_disabled = true;
 			goto exit;
 		}
 
@@ -1297,8 +1299,18 @@ static void wcd_correct_swch_plug(struct work_struct *work)
 		wcd_mbhc_adc_update_fsm_source(mbhc, plug_type);
 
 exit:
-	if (mbhc->mbhc_cb->mbhc_micbias_control/* &&  !mbhc->micbias_enable*/)
-		mbhc->mbhc_cb->mbhc_micbias_control(component, MIC_BIAS_2, MICB_DISABLE);
+	/*
+	 * Every path into this label already released exactly one
+	 * MICB_ENABLE vote: either here, or -- for HEADPHONE, and for the
+	 * hs_detect_work_stop early exit above -- via wcd_micbias_disable()
+	 * below. Releasing it twice underflows mbhc_cb->mbhc_micbias_control's
+	 * backing refcount (wcd->sysclk_users in wcd934x), which then never
+	 * reaches zero and never reaches its enable branch either.
+	 */
+	if (plug_type != MBHC_PLUG_TYPE_HEADPHONE && !micbias_disabled) {
+		if (mbhc->mbhc_cb->mbhc_micbias_control/* &&  !mbhc->micbias_enable*/)
+			mbhc->mbhc_cb->mbhc_micbias_control(component, MIC_BIAS_2, MICB_DISABLE);
+	}
 
 	/*
 	 * If plug type is corrected from special headset to headphone,
@@ -1306,7 +1318,8 @@ static void wcd_correct_swch_plug(struct work_struct *work)
 	 * disable micbias.
 	 */
 	if (plug_type == MBHC_PLUG_TYPE_HEADPHONE) {
-		wcd_micbias_disable(mbhc);
+		if (!micbias_disabled)
+			wcd_micbias_disable(mbhc);
 		/*
 		 * Enable ADC COMPLETE interrupt for HEADPHONE.
 		 * Btn release may happen after the correct work, ADC COMPLETE
